:"d050f904fa8bae0b15302ab1e0c81b5d8da170ab3076688d80b44ed993fe08d6","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/bird-search.mjs","size":3887,"sha256":"92d3c6d2d2c8ad0df431fbf866333d642a16adb89d5e2be6a6ab3c01d7ae0f26","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/features.json","size":523,"sha256":"36361f4cae0040255f84709459ebb1f0131566a567269ed7b99d073cad930f66","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/paginate-cursor.js","size":1225,"sha256":"5f20227de1d68250ad59b7ad593db4bfb1d0f1a21694963eab3ed413c2d0d5c0","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/query-ids.json","size":815,"sha256":"eba47a9d26f87d0b4eb8a4f554833ed8d11b3d8728e363deeae702d09f87fc02","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/runtime-features.js","size":5036,"sha256":"f41614d62b6c91dfc85fc4af389e6f49435324bf26460b715a991486609579d8","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/runtime-query-ids.js","size":9424,"sha256":"0f5c61dbaad3de7fb44a14c57ed005228e51f9fc361472eff59bff4cb2a1199e","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/twitter-client-base.js","size":4853,"sha256":"ea972b7894458e78edd1927d102a052ae45726a7c967b376ac7f5544f5b65499","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/twitter-client-constants.js","size":2535,"sha256":"27bd1416ff1f5d4f4516d784a8fb9ee08a87413f07b375752821a32e5b0cd6e3","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/twitter-client-features.js","size":18400,"sha256":"4b4f2048069f751a821777cb2084f3b9126d99a958494fef71f0699d8145c4dd","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/twitter-client-search.js","size":7310,"sha256":"3dfbe18ea54215d9a6393ff0884d9977dd9ddf0884a06486bdaee8a4e30d4616","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/twitter-client-types.js","size":59,"sha256":"6450f74c664db958d703e09288184ef1ca5f622782f9e11a5a9bfa3d3c78c534","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/lib/twitter-client-utils.js","size":19169,"sha256":"b230db5583760ccd0b5b5fb1592f449a7d0bc92f6184808e8ffb6f8968df20e9","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/lib/vendor/bird-search/package.json","size":331,"sha256":"96b65305969a179ee7a7735f1b475599d6035f32fda1fd030ea57ee09380cdb5","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/lib/xai_x.py","size":7110,"sha256":"d8d997f1d8b293ac829bf19532cd3c2f5ce9e6fdc223e6909e4093485e8fdb2c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/lib/xiaohongshu_api.py","size":5321,"sha256":"c7a29dfa03f871993dc13a8ad528beed8a648102404b658242ca57878077ef60","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/lib/youtube_yt.py","size":33912,"sha256":"2aa4ecad72e9aa56b77b4cc8b4cd512218ed9da4cd321f7a7c6064bdd66f0e9a","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/store.py","size":23302,"sha256":"ab2e7613337bfb7843d7f3acd88e7b4329a23134ccd38a933ffa52706c8794a0","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/watchlist.py","size":9398,"sha256":"96a9b558b586f1c42d4ff2c6d1ab7c2660d52011bc51f50b4c5440a12ce54056","contentType":"text/plain"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1776834801974,"model":"gpt-5-mini","hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4ddc08c295374affab307a485d2dd497948b608fa9deddf2a93e2d098fd5f53c","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4ddc08c295374affab307a485d2dd497948b608fa9deddf2a93e2d098fd5f53c","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: last30days-official\nVersion: 3.0.0-open\n\nThe skill is a comprehensive research and monitoring tool that aggregates data from multiple social media platforms (Reddit, X, YouTube, TikTok, Instagram) and web sources. It features a sophisticated orchestration pipeline including intelligent pre-research (auto-resolution of handles/subreddits), a SQLite-backed knowledge accumulator with full-text search, and a 'fun judge' LLM-scoring mechanism. While the skill utilizes high-privilege tools like Bash for dependency management (installing yt-dlp via Homebrew) and allows the agent to modify its own configuration file (~/.config/last30days/.env) for user-requested toggles like ELI5 mode, these behaviors are transparently documented and strictly aligned with the stated purpose. The code includes security best practices such as checking file permissions on secrets files (lib/env.py) and using structured subprocess calls rather than raw shell execution. No evidence of malicious intent, unauthorized data exfiltration, or obfuscation was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1776834801974},"skillspector":null,"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill appears to implement a legitimate multi-source research tool, but its declared metadata (no required env, no required binaries, no install) does not match the actual instructions and code which expect many API keys, local files, and platform binaries — this mismatch is concerning and needs user review before installing.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The name/description (research social/web sources, watchlist, briefings) matches the included code and references. The code contains connectors for Reddit, X, YouTube, TikTok, Instagram, Hacker News, GitHub, Perplexity, Polymarket and supports watchlists/SQLite persistence, which is coherent with the stated purpose. However, there are small inconsistencies across docs (e.g., changelog references SCRAPECREATORS_API_KEY as a primary env while SKILL.md lists OPENAI_API_KEY for Reddit), which look like versioning/maintenance drift.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"},{"detail":"SKILL.md instructs the agent to locate the skill folder, read/write multiple files, run the included Python CLI scripts, persist data to ~/.local/share/last30days/research.db and ~/.local/share/last30days/briefs, save reports to ~/Documents/Last30Days, and optionally run setup/device-auth flows. It also instructs always using --auto-resolve and running long-running networked searches. The skill will read and write user files and may perform network requests; these behaviors are broader than the skill's declared metadata (which lists no env vars or binaries).","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Registry metadata shows no install spec and 'required binaries: none', but the shipped code expects Node.js (vendored bird-search .mjs executed via node) and mentions yt-dlp for YouTube. The package vendors JS code and launches subprocesses (node, possibly yt-dlp). This disparity (no declared binary requirements yet requiring node/yt-dlp) is an incoherence and increases risk because the runtime will spawn subprocesses with environment injection.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The registry claims no required environment variables or credentials, but SKILL.md and code clearly expect multiple API keys and tokens (OPENAI_API_KEY, XAI_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, PARALLEL_API_KEY, BRAVE_API_KEY, SCRAPECREATORS_API_KEY, and X auth tokens AUTH_TOKEN/CT0). The skill also reads/writes a local ~/.config/last30days/.env and can inject those values into subprocesses. Requiring platform account tokens (especially AUTH_TOKEN/CT0 for X) and multiple LLM/web-search keys is broad and not declared — the requested secrets are disproportionate to the metadata and warrant caution.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill persists data to a local SQLite DB (~/.local/share/last30days/research.db), writes briefing JSON to ~/.local/share/last30days/briefs and Markdown to ~/Documents/Last30Days, and offers watchlist automation instructions (cron/launchd). It also contains a setup wizard that can write config and device-auth info. Persisting research, tokens, and saved outputs is functional for the feature but is a material persistence/privilege increase compared to the declared empty requirements and should be considered before granting credentials or enabling scheduled runs.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"This skill includes substantial runnable code and persistent storage but the registry metadata (no required env vars or binaries; no install) does not reflect that. Before installing or providing credentials: 1) Inspect and run the built-in diagnostic: python3 <skill_root>/scripts/last30days.py --diagnose to see which sources require keys and which binaries are missing. 2) Do NOT paste account tokens (AUTH_TOKEN/CT0 or others) unless you understand the risk — X tokens can grant access to your account data. Prefer read-only or scoped keys where possible. 3) If you want to try safely, run the scripts in an isolated environment (container or throwaway VM) and avoid writing secrets to ~/.config until satisfied. 4) Verify required binaries (node, yt-dlp) are acceptable to install on your system — node is required to run the vendored bird-search module. 5) Be cautious about enabling cron/automatic runs or running the setup/device-auth flows; those will persist configuration and may schedule recurring networked activity. 6) If you plan to use the skill, consider limiting credential scope, reviewing the vendored JS (bird-search.mjs), and confirming which backend (ScrapeCreators vs OpenAI/Perplexity/OpenRouter) the current variant actually uses (there are conflicting references).","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":"gpt-5-mini","checkedAt":1775671096144}}}}}